 "description": "Leloup1998_CircClock_LD\nBioModels BIOMD0000000171 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000171_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 300 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000171_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: oscillating), sampling 0.3.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 5.83e-06 of species peak (worst: T2)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] species 'Tt' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] species 'Pt' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] M_T_decay term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] M_P_decay term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] P_pho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] P1_pho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] P1_depho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] P2_depho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] T_pho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] T1_pho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] T1_depho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] T2_depho: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+